@startuml
title Trace representation in the search: <latex>\Theta(d)</latex> copying per edge becomes <latex>\Theta(1)</latex> sharing

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
}

rectangle "TODAY — `Node.trace: Vec<RendezvousName>`" as A #FEE2E2 {
  rectangle "node at depth 1\n""[ n0 ]""" as A1 #FECACA
  rectangle "node at depth 2\n""[ n0, n1 ]""\n<i>n0 COPIED</i>" as A2 #FECACA
  rectangle "node at depth 3\n""[ n0, n1, n2 ]""\n<i>n0, n1 COPIED</i>" as A3 #FECACA
  rectangle "sibling at depth 3\n""[ n0, n1, n2' ]""\n<i>n0, n1 COPIED AGAIN</i>" as A3b #FECACA
  A1 -down-> A2
  A2 -down-> A3
  A2 -down-> A3b
}

note right of A3b
  `extend_from_slice` copies every ancestor,
  **two heap allocations per copied element**.

  One line of depth <latex>D</latex> therefore costs
  <latex>\Theta(D^2)</latex>, and the whole tree
  <latex>\Theta(E \cdot d)</latex>.
end note

rectangle "PROPOSED — `Option<Arc<TraceStep>>`" as B #DCFCE7 {
  rectangle "**TraceStep**\nstep: `d0`\ndepth: 0\nparent: NIL" as B0 #BBF7D0
  rectangle "**TraceStep**\nstep: `d1`\ndepth: 1" as B1 #BBF7D0
  rectangle "**TraceStep**\nstep: `d2`\ndepth: 2" as B2 #BBF7D0
  rectangle "**TraceStep**\nstep: `d2'`\ndepth: 2" as B2b #BBF7D0

  B1 -up-> B0 : parent
  B2 -up-> B1 : parent
  B2b -up-> B1 : parent
}

note right of B2b
  A child is **one** ""Arc::new"" plus a refcount
  bump — <latex>\Theta(1)</latex> per edge, whatever the depth.

  Siblings SHARE their ancestors instead of
  copying them; the chain is immutable, so it is
  safe to hold across the search's ""await"" points.

  ""MATERIALISE"" runs <latex>\Theta(d)</latex> once per DELIVERED
  LEAF — <latex>\Theta(E) + \Theta(L \cdot d)</latex> in total.
end note

A -[#DC2626,thickness=2]-> B : copy-on-extend\nbecomes\npoint-at-parent

@enduml
